---
import ChapterLayout from '../../../layouts/ChapterLayout.astro';
import { getDrakeChapter } from '../../../data/story/drakeChaptersData';
import { processDrakeContentHtml } from '../../../utils/drakeContentProcessor';

const chapter = getDrakeChapter('013-light', 'chapter-3')!;

const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/')
  ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL
  : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;

const rawContentHtml = "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Part 12, Chapter 3, the moment you've all been waiting for! Well, I have.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#The_Esperkin\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">The Esperkin</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#A_New_Ally\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">A New Ally</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Dream_of_the_Future\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Dream of the Future</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#The_Lady&#39;s_Crystal\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">The Lady's Crystal</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Esperkin\">The Esperkin</span><a title=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: The Esperkin\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Part_12?action=edit&amp;section=1\" aria-label=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: The Esperkin\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>New character, naturally, and what a character!\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>PLAYABLE CHARACTER - <b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Terra_Branford_(Dissidia_PSP)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Terra Branford (Dissidia PSP)\">Terra</a></b>\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-left\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/1d/Dissidia_Terra.png/revision/latest?cb=20101110154919\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"Dissidia Terra\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/1d/Dissidia_Terra.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/175?cb=20101110154919\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"175\" height=\"295\" class=\"mw-file-element\" data-image-name=\"Dissidia Terra.png\" data-image-key=\"Dissidia_Terra.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Oh my lovely Terra, good to see you at last! Terra is, for those of you not familiar with me, one of my all-time favorite Final Fantasy characters, narrowly edged out of the #1 slot by a hero we'll get to later in the game. A beautiful, powerful, determined, heroic warrior-mage, Terra is all kinds of awesome...in Final Fantasy VI. Unfortunately she kinda got shafted in the Dissidia games, her determination and protectiveness are toned down and her self-doubt and insecurities are played up, to the point of, as you saw in Vaan's chapter, temporarily wishing for death to avoid being used by Kefka anymore. They cast Onion Knight as her protector, when to keep to the spirit of VI, <i>she</i> should have been vowing to protect <i>him</i>. Dissidia 012 tweaks the dialogue in both their stories to have more emphasis on a mutual friendship between them, as well as to show her heroic spirit and determination more, but the 12th cycle more than made up for that. So between games her character arc has a higher end point, but a lower start. At least they tried, didn't quite work but they did try.\n</p><p>That misrepresentation of her carries over into gameplay, but that is not to say she's weak and helpless, it's just that she focuses on magic while in VI she was also a strong physical fighter too. Terra is one of my favorite characters in the game to play as, she was one of the strongest in the original Dissidia but got heavily nerfed in this game, her three bread-and-butter attacks (Blizzara, Blizzard Combo, Holy Combo) getting reduced range, tracking and/or power. She's still perfectly powerful though, possessing powerful magic combos that combo very well with Assists, and she has a very well-rounded moveset, preferring to fight from long range in the air but having a few good options for close-quarters and ground combat. Blizzard Combo is a fairly quick melee attack with good power, it's Terra's core \"back off, I'm a mage and like keeping my distance\" attack. Blizzara is a very powerful ranged attack that inflicts Wall Rush, it's range kinda sucks though. Fire sends a burst of flame along the ground that explodes over a small radius to begin a Chase, it packs a surprising punch, generates the most EX Force of her attacks, and isn't slow to execute, but isn't very fast either. Finally Thundaga summons four converging lightning bolts around the opponent, easy to dodge but like Shift Break is good to punish opponents trying to charge up an attack since they can't avoid it. \n</p><p>Her initial HP attacks are Flood, which summons a blast of water below the opponent, also good for charging opponents if you're on the ground at the time but useless otherwise since it's slow to activate, and Tornado, a close-range attack that summons a trio of whirlwinds to cycle Terra before combining into one to slamming the opponent into the air, sucking them in for the duration and deflecting projectiles - it has melee damage priority so even the likes of Cloud's Braver and Lightning's Crushing Blow just causes both Terra and them to stagger rather than have them pierce it to hit her. It's slow to start up and has a very long end-lag that makes it easy to punish her, as I've noted in the instances where you've fought her or her manikins, but in close quarters in small areas like Pandaemonium or Kefka's Tower, it's a nightmare. She levels up she diversifies her moveset with more utility attacks, including what was, in the original Dissidia, one of the most powerful combos in the entire game and is still lethal, but we'll get to those when she learns them.\n</p><p>To repeat, Terra is one of my favorite characters to fight as and one of my most favorite actual characters. Enjoy using her to rain magical chaos on your enemies.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>I once again bought Terra three extra accessories slots and gave her a Hyper Ring, Earring, Sunrise, HP = 100%, Level 1-9, and BRV ≥ Base Value. For equipment, a Snowscepter, Mythril Bangle, Mythril Hairpin, and Silken Shirt. Launch the story now. Terra is a bit worried since she suddenly has trouble sensing things, and when Onion Knight says he'll protect her. She's surprised at the shift of behavior and thinks she feels she's forgetting something important.\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Valor Incense\"><img alt=\"Valor Incense\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"1994 gil\"><img alt=\"1994 gil\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">2\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Phantasmal Girl\"><img alt=\"Phantasmal Girl\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">3\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"DFF Start\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Start.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Start.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/8f/D012_Emblem_Blue.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209004544\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Booster Accessory x5\"><img alt=\"Booster Accessory x5\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Emblem Blue.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Emblem_Blue.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/8f/D012_Emblem_Blue.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209004544\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">4\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Phantasmal Harlequin\"><img alt=\"Phantasmal Harlequin\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Counterfeit Youth\"><img alt=\"Counterfeit Youth\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/73/DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png/revision/latest?cb=20141117182922\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Stigma of Chaos\"><img alt=\"Stigma of Chaos\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"39\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Stigma Of Chaos.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/73/DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/39?cb=20141117182922\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Idle Sky Pirate\"><img alt=\"Idle Sky Pirate\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><div style=\"overflow:hidden;float:left;margin:0 1px\"><div style=\"position:relative;left:-0px;margin-right:-25px;top:-30px;margin-bottom:-30px;;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/f/f7/Dissicon_ff3_OK1.png/revision/latest?cb=20111011032221\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"Dissicon ff3 OK1\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"61\" height=\"70\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"Dissicon ff3 OK1.png\" data-image-key=\"Dissicon_ff3_OK1.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/f/f7/Dissicon_ff3_OK1.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/61?cb=20111011032221\" /></a></span></div></div>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Jump Chain at D3 to get three of them, using the Booster x5 emblem. The bonus line is 2, which Terra will meet if you did the Report featuring her after Vaan's story, and the KP Chance is a 90 second victory. Onion Knight is our Assist, his aerial Assist is his aerial Bravery attack, driving the opponent up into the ceiling. His ground Assist is Blizzard-Blizzaga, beginning an Assist Chase...teleport...I'm gonna have to look up the official term come to think of it, I don't know. \n</p><p>First up is a Phantasmal Girl with Fire, Blizzara, Flood, and the Alexander summon, fortunately it's Auto so she only gets to use it if she Breaks you. She also has the accessory gimmick for this storyline, a Pearl Necklace, Attractorb and Dragonfly Orb with six Break boosters, meaning once you Break them it's an 11.3x booster to those accessories. Wave \"hello\" to their EX Gauge filling up at a rapid rate. Next is a Phantasmal Harlequin with the two Blizzaga attacks, Havoc Wing, those same accessories, and an unknown summon. Third and last is a Counterfeit Youth, it has Blizzard, Blizzaga, and the aerial melee attack and its follow-up. The enemy left over is an Idle Sky Pirate, I beat it up with great gusto, it uses Crossbow and Shield &amp; Sword. At Level 4 Terra learns the ground version of Blizzara, might as well use it for now.\n</p><p>The two chests simply have a Valor Incense and 1994 gil. As we leave Terra is concerned that she hasn't found her Crystal yet, and the Onion Knight relays what Golbez and Cosmos taught him about following his heart to find the Crystal. Terra isn't sure what her heart wants yet, but the Knight is sure it'll come to her in time.\n</p><p>On the world map now, Terra makes a nice little nod to her original game if you talk to the Onion Knight, the devs again including a geological mythology gag. The chest on the island behind us has 500 gil. If you don't get one from the orbs of the dead, buy a Straight Chain and a Multichain from the moogle, he otherwise has nothing worth buying unless you're 100 KP richer than me, in which case buy the Flame Rod for Terra and use it over the Snowscepter, it has higher power and further boosts her magic damage a bit. Near the moogle is a Phantasmal Harlequin, it just uses Hyperdrive and has three Cursed Rings, no danger here. The chest behind it has a BRV Zero skill. The outcropping of land below the castle has a Pink Tail, haven't found many of those lately have we? Before heading into the mountains to the next gateway, make a left to find an Assist Charge, and go up the path near the gateway to find a Rosetta Stone.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"A_New_Ally\">A New Ally</span><a title=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: A New Ally\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Part_12?action=edit&amp;section=2\" aria-label=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: A New Ally\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Phantasmal Girl\"><img alt=\"Phantasmal Girl\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/73/DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png/revision/latest?cb=20141117182922\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Stigma of Chaos\"><img alt=\"Stigma of Chaos\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"39\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Stigma Of Chaos.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/73/DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/39?cb=20141117182922\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">2\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Idle Sky Pirate\"><img alt=\"Idle Sky Pirate\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">3\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span