</a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">4\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/13/D012_Emblem_Purple.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050509\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Initial BRV Boostm\"><img alt=\"Initial BRV Boostm\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Emblem Purple.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Emblem_Purple.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/13/D012_Emblem_Purple.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050509\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/13/D012_Emblem_Purple.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050509\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"KP +1\"><img alt=\"KP +1\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Emblem Purple.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Emblem_Purple.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/13/D012_Emblem_Purple.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050509\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/d/d3/Dissicon_ff7_Clo1.png/revision/latest?cb=20110126030954\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Assist Character\"><img alt=\"Assist Character\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"Dissicon ff7 Clo1.png\" data-image-key=\"Dissicon_ff7_Clo1.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/d/d3/Dissicon_ff7_Clo1.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110126030954\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Phantasmal Girl\"><img alt=\"Phantasmal Girl\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235702\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Kefka Palazzo\"><img alt=\"Kefka Palazzo\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"36\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chaos Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chaos_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/36?cb=20110203235702\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Cross Chain at E4 or Jump Chain at F4. The first gives you an initial Bravery boost to get the fights over with, the second is a KP +1, so the chain will earn 18 KP as opposed to the Cross Chain's 16, up to 19 with the KP for beating the last enemy. 3 KP isn't much but you never know when you'll be a few KP short so it can't hurt. The bonus line is 16 and the KP Chance is a 90 second win. As always for bosses, charge your EX Gauge as much as you can before killing your foes each fight.\n</p><p>With the Jump Chain, a Phantasmal Harlequin is first, it has Havoc Wing and the Blizzagas, of course. Next, a Delusory Dragoon with Lance Burst, Lance Barrage, and Jump. Jump is always a bit tricky to deal with but still not much of a problem for you unless you try using Flood, since it lasts so long you won't be able to dodge. Now all that's left is a Phantasmal Girl with Blizzara and Flood, as well as those EX accessories. She also has an Assist, but how often does the AI attack enough to actually use their Assists? The last foe not chained is the one guarding the chest, a Transient Witch with Land Worm, the EX accessories, Knight's Axe, Great Attractor, and a Phantasmal Girl Assist. \n</p><p>The chest has 1000 gil for us. I also unlocked new shop items - trade accessories! Yes, a lot (not all but a lot) of trade accessories can be snagged in the shop by trading Elixir-type items, the Dusty Elixir, Elixir, Hi-Elixir and Megalixir. In Confessions of the Creator there's a moogle that sells the lesser trade materials but that's a bit further down the road. I have a single Dusty Elixir, maybe you have two or three. The trade accessories needed are for various Level 1 and Level 30 equipment pieces. Let's examine what's available to us, since the items that need trade accessories are stronger than the ones only need cash. Not I'm only going to cover the Level 1 items you probably haven't unlocked yet, if I know you have then I won't mention them.\n</p><p>The Zweihander needs a Bangaa Tooth, it has 24 power, making it one of the strongest weapons you have at the moment, and further boosts physical damage by 3%, but as a Greatsword some characters can't make use of it like Terra, Onion Knight's etc. Triton's Dagger needs Chocobo Chick Powder, 20 Attack and gives +5% EX Force at the start of each fight. Don't we have two Cyan Drops that give 10% each? Yes we do. Moving on. I mention the Slasher and the Figaro Gravel needed for it only for the sake of being comprehensive, it sucks. The Dwarven Axe has a whopping 26 power, but it needs a 3-Elixir item and can only be used by a handful of heroes so we'll skip it. The Full Metal staff has 22 power and boosts magic damage by 3%, but once Terra is done there's no more mages in the storyline and while some of the heroes can use staffs they're physical fighters and thus have better options. The Chakram has 26 power, grants an extra 3% from EX force you absorb, and can be used by a few heroes, but skip it for better options I say. The Six-Fluted Pole <i>is</i> good for stats, 20 attack and a nice +15 Assist charge at the start of each fight, the problem is that it needs a a Cypress Pole to trade, and thus you need a Mu Fur and Moogle Fur requiring 3 Dusty Elixirs total. Ouch. Your choice kiddies. \n</p><p>There's nothing too awesome for armor, and even if there was our ultimate goal now is to get enough Mythril to use three Mythril items for armor with a weapon of course choice.\n</p>\n<table style=\"width: 275px; D012 article-table; text-align: center; color:black; float:right\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"font-size: larger; background:#1E90FF\" colspan=\"6\"><font color=\"white\"><b>Boss</b></font>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Kefka_Palazzo_(Dissidia_PSP)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Kefka Palazzo (Dissidia PSP)\">Kefka</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/e/e0/DissidiaKefkaRender.png/revision/latest?cb=20110216225812\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"DissidiaKefkaRender\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"100\" height=\"137\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DissidiaKefkaRender.png\" data-image-key=\"DissidiaKefkaRender.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/e/e0/DissidiaKefkaRender.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/100?cb=20110216225812\" /></a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>HP</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Level</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Bravery</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"2\">3,282\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">20\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">363\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>Brave Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Twisty-Turny Blizzaga, Scatter Spray Blizzaga, Waggle-Wobbly Firaga, Meteor, Extra-Crispy Firaga, Lickity-Split Thundaga\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>HP Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Hyperdrive, Havoc Wing, Trine\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Summon</b>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Difficulty</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"3\">Brynhildr\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\">1/5\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>As we engage the end piece, Terra refuses to join Kefka, who rolls out the Cloud of Darkness to attack them. The Onion Knight arrives, having somehow freed himself, and he and Cloud take on the Cloud of Darkness, leaving Terra to deal with Kefka.\n</p><p>Kefka has a nice equipment set-up and decent boosters, an Earring with 4 1.2 Far From Opponent. He's also got an Idle Sky Pirate Assist, and you have none. But by now you are very well-versed in how to deal with his attacks and can spam Thundara to keep him on the ropes. As you know many of his attacks have start-up lag and have him hold still for the duration, so Thundara is his bane and can halt him in his tracks most every time. Keep your distance to avoid his faster attacks like Scatter-Spray Blizzaga and Lickity-Split Thundaga, and he's a piece of cake. The initial Break and Wall Rush for HP hit will only knock off around half his HP, let him recovery his Bravery, then blast him with an HP hit and use your EX Burst. As you land the first hit he'll summon Brynhildr, double the Bravery pool, and thus the EX Burst will Break him and do enough damage to kill him for sure.\n</p><p>With Kefka given a painful reminder that you don't fuck with the Esperkin Goddess of Magic, he retreats, and Terra receives her Crystal, and the three heroes set out to find the others. The quest is still not over.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<table class=\"toccolours\" width=\"85%\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; margin:0 auto; text-align: center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align: center; border:solid 1px\"><b><a href=\"/story/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake\">Drake Clawfang's Dissidia 012 Walkthrough</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"10%\" style=\"border:solid 1px\" rowspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-2/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 11\">Previous page</a></b>\n</td>\n<td>\n<table width=\"100%\" style=\"text-align:center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Treachery_of_the_Gods\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Treachery of the Gods\">Treachery of the Gods</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/story/012-treachery/prologue-chapter-1/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 1\">Prologue / Chapter 1</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-2/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 2\">2</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-3/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 3\">3</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-4/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 4\">4</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-5/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 5\">5</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-6/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 6\">6</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-7/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 7\">7</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/epilogue/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 8\">Epilogue</a><hr />\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Light_to_All\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Light to All\">Light to All</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/story/013-light/prologue/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 9\">Prologue</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-1/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 10\">Chapter 1</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-2/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 11\">2</a> - <strong class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</strong> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-4/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 13\">4</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-5/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 14\">5</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-6/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 15\">6</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-7/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 16\">7</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-8/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 17\">8</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-9/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 18\">9</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-10/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 19\">10</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/epilogue-part-1/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 20\">Epilogue Part 1</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/epilogue-part-2/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 21\">Part 2</a><hr />\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td width=\"10%\" style=\"border:solid 1px\" rowspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-4/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 13\">Next page</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<table width=\"100%\" style=\"text-align:center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" valign=\"top\">\n<table width=\"100%\" style=\"text-align:center\">\n<caption><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Confessions_of_the_Creator\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Confessions of the Creator\">Confessions of the Creator</a></b>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><a href=\"/story/000-creator/southern-areas/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 22\">Part 1</a> - <a href=\"/story/000-creator/shantotto-and-gabranth/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 23\">Part 2</a> - <a href=\"/story/000-creator/chasm-of-earth-and-flying-castle/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 24\">Part 3</a> - <a href=\"/story/000-creator/gaia-and-bahamut-isles/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 25\">Part 